# Thread t of CTA c stores when t + 64·c < 1000. With no grid, %ctaid is
# unbounded and the mask an unknown selector. Under 15 CTAs every thread
# of every CTA stores, so the guard holds; under 16 the last CTA stores
# on its first 40 threads, so per CTA the store is a bound, and over the
# launch it is 1000 threads' 4000 B. Under the largest grid CUDA allows,
# 2^31-1 by 65535 by 65535 CTAs, a count over the launch leaves i64 and
# is unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_mask.ptx --bind 1:n=1000 | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_mask.ptx --bind 1:n=1000 --grid 15 | FileCheck --check-prefix=FULL "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_mask.ptx --bind 1:n=1000 --grid 16 | FileCheck --check-prefix=PARTIAL "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_mask.ptx --bind 1:n=1000 --grid 2147483647,65535,65535 | FileCheck --check-prefix=HUGE "%s"
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)  warp: <= 5 sectors (ideal <= 4)
FREE: totals per CTA [static]:
FREE: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 256 B
FULL: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)  warp: 4–5 sectors (ideal 4)
FULL: totals per CTA [static]:
FULL: global bytes: load 0 B, store 256 B
PARTIAL: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 64 threads in 2 warps (%tid.x + 64 * %ctaid.x < 1000)  warp: <= 5 sectors (ideal <= 4)
PARTIAL: totals per CTA [static]:
PARTIAL: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 256 B
PARTIAL: totals per launch [static]:
PARTIAL: global bytes: load 0 B, store 4000 B
HUGE: totals per launch [static]:
HUGE: instructions = 0 + unknown
HUGE: global bytes: load 0 B, store 0 B + unknown
